# Build targets & toolchain

## SDK version matrix

| Target        | SDK version | CPU             | Unit format        |
|---------------|-------------|-----------------|--------------------|
| NTS-1 mkI     | v1.1.0      | ARM Cortex-M4   | Static ELF         |
| Minilogue XD  | v1.1.0      | ARM Cortex-M4   | Static ELF         |
| Prologue      | v1.1.0      | ARM Cortex-M4   | Static ELF         |
| NTS-1 mkII    | v2.0.0      | ARM Cortex-M7   | Dynamic .so        |
| NTS-3         | v2.0.0      | ARM Cortex-M7   | Dynamic .so        |

**NTS-1 mkI, Minilogue XD, and Prologue units are binary-compatible**
when built with the same SDK version.

## Build files required per unit

1. `project.mk` — points to SDK, sets `PROJECT`, `SOURCES`, `TARGET`.
2. `manifest.json` — unit metadata and parameter declarations.
3. `Makefile` — sets `PLATFORMDIR` and includes the SDK platform makefile.

## Build command

From repo root (recommended):

```bash
./tools/build.sh oscillators/template nutekt-digital
```

From a unit directory (after `PLATFORMDIR` or `LOGUE_SDK` is set):

```bash
make
```

## Toolchain

- GNU Arm Embedded Toolchain (provided in `tools/gcc/` of the logue SDK).
- MSYS2 on Windows for GNU Make and shell utilities.
- Docker (optional) — use the official logue-sdk container for reproducible builds.

## Web simulator (NTS-1 mkII / NTS-3)

The SDK includes a web-based simulator (`websim/`) that lets you test DSP
code in a browser without flashing hardware. Use it for fast iteration on
algorithm logic before building for hardware.
